cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the repository and the exact commit used."
title: "StillHere: pilot the story before booking the scanner"
abstract: "A first healthy reference for a new story, before any scans, and evidence for how far to trust it. StillHere plans a listening study from a tested menu with Muse Spark 1.3, builds and checks the stimulus with Muse Voice Transcribe, forecasts the healthy-adult brain response with Meta's TRIBE v2, and shows how forecasts did on real public scans. Research use; healthy volunteers and public data only; not a diagnosis or medical advice."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Aryen
    given-names: Raghav
repository-code: "https://github.com/Yatsuiii/stillhere"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - functional MRI
  - naturalistic stimuli
  - brain encoding model
  - TRIBE v2
  - pre-registration
  - stimulus checks
